+### audio_capture
+
+<table>
+    <tr>
+        <td>Description</td>
+        <td colspan="2">
+            Which audio is streamed. When empty, the whole audio sink is captured.
+            With `onscreen`, only the applications that have a window visible on the streamed display are
+            captured, using per-process loopback; voice chat applications such as Discord are never captured.
+            The host keeps playing audio on its own speakers.
+            @note{Windows 10 2004 or later. Falls back to the whole sink when unavailable.}
+        </td>
+    </tr>
+    <tr>
+        <td>Default</td>
+        <td colspan="2">n/a</td>
+    </tr>
+    <tr>
+        <td>Example</td>
+        <td colspan="2">@code{}
+            audio_capture = onscreen
+            @endcode</td>
+    </tr>
+</table>
+
+### audio_exclude_apps
+
+<table>
+    <tr>
+        <td>Description</td>
+        <td colspan="2">
+            Comma-separated executables that are never captured when [audio_capture](#audio_capture) is
+            `onscreen`, in addition to the built-in voice chat applications.
+        </td>
+    </tr>
+    <tr>
+        <td>Default</td>
+        <td colspan="2">n/a</td>
+    </tr>
+    <tr>
+        <td>Example</td>
+        <td colspan="2">@code{}
+            audio_exclude_apps = spotify.exe, obs64.exe
+            @endcode</td>
+    </tr>
+</table>
